# What must never reach the build context.
#
# The first two entries are the ones that matter, and they are the same two
# rules CLAUDE.md rule 5 states for git: no card pool, no credentials. `.git`
# would carry both back in through history, which is why it is excluded rather
# than merely unused.

# The pool and everything derived from it. Scryfall asks that bulk data not
# be redistributed, and the volume is where it lives. A local `data/` here is
# ~600MB, so this is also the difference between a fast build and a slow one.
data/

# Credentials. `.env` is gitignored, so it exists only locally — which is
# exactly the file a build context would otherwise pick up and bake in.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# History carries deleted files. Nothing in the image needs it.
.git/
.github/

# Node's tree and the frontend source. The image installs the *committed*
# bundle at `web_dist/`; `web/` is what CI rebuilds it from.
web/

# Local Python state. `.venv` is a macOS x86 virtualenv and would be both huge
# and useless in a linux/arm64 image.
.venv/
**/__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
.mypy_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.hypothesis/
.coverage
htmlcov/
build/
dist/
*.egg-info/

# Tests, docs and planning documents. The image runs the app; CI runs the
# suite, from a checkout rather than from a layer.
#
# `*.md` is root-level only — a single `*` does not cross a `/` — which keeps
# CLAUDE.md and ROADMAP.md out without reaching into subdirectories.
tests/
docs/
*.md

# Decks. Live app data (ADR 30) — gitignored, so a checkout has none, but a
# local working copy does and it must never reach a layer: the volume is the
# only copy an instance should ever have.
decks/

# Forge's distribution, if it was ever unpacked in-tree. Several hundred MB,
# and `res/cardsfolder` is card pool data by another name.
forge/
*.jar

# Editor and OS noise.
.DS_Store
.idea/
.vscode/

# The scribe's compiled classes. It is built inside the image against the very
# jar that image ships (ADR 42), so a local `scribe/out` reaching the context
# could only ever be a stale copy compiled against a different Forge.
scribe/out/
